{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>I will heap upon them evils.</b> I will pile evil upon evil — like ״סְפוּ שָׁנָה עַל שָׁנָה״ (Isaiah 29), ״סְפוֹת הָרָוָה״ (Deuteronomy 29), ״עֹלוֹתֵיכֶם סְפוּ עַל זִבְחֵיכֶם״ (Jeremiah 7). Another interpretation — <b>אַסְפָּה</b>: I will consume — like ״פֶּן תִּסָּפֶה״ (Genesis 19)." "<b>I will spend My arrows on them.</b> All My arrows I will complete in them — and this curse, relative to the curse of blessing, is: My arrows are spent but they are not spent (Sifrei; Sotah 9)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:21.020131756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}